cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Sarcoma Epigenomic Data Atlas
message: >-
  If you use this atlas, please cite it. Please also cite the SASS Epigenetics
  Working Group white paper once it appears.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Gryder
    given-names: Berkley
    affiliation: Case Western Reserve University
repository-code: "https://github.com/<user>/sarcoma-epigenomic-atlas"
abstract: >-
  A sample-level census of every publicly recorded epigenomic experiment on
  sarcoma, all ages, spanning 16,337 de-duplicated samples across 885 studies
  and 45 named diagnostic entities. Harvested from GEO, ArrayExpress, ENA, EGA
  and the St Jude Childhood Solid Tumor Network, classified to the resolution of
  one assay on one model in one study, and joined to curated disease incidence
  so coverage can be read against burden. Separates open data from
  controlled-access holdings and from genuine absence. Includes a recovery of
  the entity labels for GSE140686, the largest sarcoma epigenomic deposit in
  existence, which is published without a diagnosis on any sample.
keywords:
  - sarcoma
  - epigenomics
  - ChIP-seq
  - ATAC-seq
  - DNA methylation
  - rhabdomyosarcoma
  - data reuse
  - FAIR data
license: CC-BY-4.0
